From e5d9dbbc5b9463c504826364d8574197b317d094 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 08:50:01 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fwupdate: signature failure explains itself + explicit
 type-to-confirm override

Owner asks: fail loudly with an explanation, and allow an override that
cannot happen by accident.

- A refused signature surfaced as the same generic check-failed text as a
  network error. The check script now sets webs_state_error=9 (stock uses
  1-3) on a signature refusal and the page shows RFWU_49: the list was
  refused because its signature is missing/wrong, briefly expected right
  after a publish (the list is signed as a final step), and if persistent
  the source may be compromised. (First attempt reused RFWU_48, which
  already means 'Standard' on the variant card - caught, renumbered.)

- Beside that message an Override... button opens the themed danger
  dialog with a NEW reaperConfirm typed-gate (opts.typed): the confirm
  button stays disabled until the user types OVERRIDE exactly - no Enter,
  no accidental click-through. Confirming sets reaper_fwsig_override=1
  (defaults.c-registered so saveNvram accepts it) and re-runs the check;
  the script consumes the flag ONE-SHOT (cleared whether needed or not),
  logs 'SIGNATURE OVERRIDE - proceeding with an UNVERIFIED manifest at
  the admin's explicit request', and proceeds. The page then brands the
  offer persistently: 'Signature override active - the update information
  below is UNVERIFIED' - the warning does not clear on success.

Dicts RFWU_49-53, lockstep 6767 x25. Host-validated: typed-gate harness
(locked initially, locked click inert, wrong case stays locked, exact
word unlocks, teardown clean), modal regression still passes, page +
util JS parse clean, ASCII 0, check script sh -n clean.
